---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const repo = 'https://github.com/charifmahmoudi/mobile-ot-security-assessment';
---
<SiteLayout title="Safety & Trust — Atlas OT Scout" description="Atlas uses bounded authorization, passive-first evidence collection, exact active operations, explicit limitations and open engineering contracts.">
  <section class="bg-ink text-white"><div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-5 py-20 sm:px-8 lg:py-28"><p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-atlas">Safety &amp; Trust</p><h1 class="mt-5 max-w-4xl text-5xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.05em] sm:text-6xl">Evidence collection should not create a new operational risk.</h1><p class="mt-7 max-w-2xl text-lg leading-8 text-white/60">Atlas is designed around explicit authority, least-intrusive evidence collection, review before acceptance, and limitations that remain visible in the final result.</p></div></section>
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-5 py-20 sm:px-8"><div class="grid gap-px overflow-hidden rounded-3xl border border-ink/10 bg-ink/10 md:grid-cols-2">{[['Authorization before transmission','Packet-producing behavior must stay inside the approved case scope and operation.'],['Passive first','Imported or mirrored evidence is preferred when it can answer the documented question.'],['Exact active operations','The initial bounded active path is one Modbus/TCP Read Device Identification request to one exact authorized target—not a subnet or port scan.'],['Evidence before conclusions','Raw observations, identity claims and accepted inventory decisions remain distinct so uncertainty can be reviewed.'],['Offline workflow','The core assessment workflow does not depend on a cloud service to collect, reconcile or hand off evidence.'],['Limitations stay visible','Visibility gaps, insufficient evidence and unresolved conflicts remain part of the result rather than being converted into certainty.']].map(([title,copy], i) => (<article class="bg-paper p-7 sm:p-8"><span class="font-mono text-xs text-atlas">0{i+1}</span><h2 class="mt-7 text-2xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.025em]">{title}</h2><p class="mt-4 max-w-xl leading-7 text-steel">{copy}</p></article>))}</div></section>
  <section class="bg-surface"><div class="mx-auto grid max-w-7xl gap-12 px-5 py-20 sm:px-8 lg:grid-cols-[.75fr_1.25fr]"><div><p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-steel">Technical review</p><h2 class="mt-4 text-4xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.04em]">The exact contracts are public.</h2><p class="mt-5 leading-7 text-steel">The website summarizes the approach. Technical reviewers can inspect the current implementation, network contract, threat model and test evidence directly.</p></div><div class="grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2"><a class="rounded-2xl border border-ink/10 bg-paper p-5 hover:border-atlas/40" href={`${repo}/blob/main/IMPLEMENTATION.md`}><strong>Implementation status</strong><span class="mt-2 block text-sm leading-6 text-steel">What executes today and what remains deferred.</span></a><a class="rounded-2xl border border-ink/10 bg-paper p-5 hover:border-atlas/40" href={`${repo}/blob/main/docs/architecture/NETWORK-EXECUTION.md`}><strong>Network execution</strong><span class="mt-2 block text-sm leading-6 text-steel">Exact active/passive behavior and stop boundaries.</span></a><a class="rounded-2xl border border-ink/10 bg-paper p-5 hover:border-atlas/40" href={`${repo}/blob/main/docs/architecture/SECURITY-AND-THREAT-MODEL.md`}><strong>Security model</strong><span class="mt-2 block text-sm leading-6 text-steel">Threats, controls and residual risks.</span></a><a class="rounded-2xl border border-ink/10 bg-paper p-5 hover:border-atlas/40" href={`${repo}/tree/main/docs/testing`}><strong>Verification evidence</strong><span class="mt-2 block text-sm leading-6 text-steel">CI topology, testbeds and proof boundaries.</span></a></div></div></section>
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-5 py-20 sm:px-8"><div class="rounded-3xl border border-signal/30 bg-signal/[.07] p-7 sm:p-9"><p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-signal">Current status</p><h2 class="mt-4 text-2xl font-semibold">P0-WATER is progressing toward controlled customer-pilot qualification.</h2><p class="mt-4 leading-7 text-steel">This site describes the product method and target pilot contract. Current executable capabilities and remaining release gates are maintained in the repository rather than inferred from marketing material.</p><div class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap gap-3"><a class="rounded-full bg-ink px-5 py-2.5 text-sm font-semibold text-white" href={`${repo}/blob/main/IMPLEMENTATION.md`}>Current implementation</a><a class="rounded-full border border-ink/15 px-5 py-2.5 text-sm font-semibold" href={`${repo}/blob/main/ROADMAP.md`}>Roadmap</a></div></div><p class="mt-10 text-center text-sm text-steel">Considering a bounded evaluation? <a class="font-semibold text-ink underline decoration-atlas/40 underline-offset-4" href={`${base}pilot/`}>Review the pilot model.</a></p></section>
</SiteLayout>
